body:
SaveManager loses its unsaved-state flag after a storage failure. This is present on main `d4e4ac69bbd93d237eaf5d0260bc6a5ff3a5e373` and also in #2077. The exit-save fix in #2077 does not introduce this behavior and correctly retains the project on an explicit save failure.

### Reproduction using the actual manager

Run Node26 from `frontend` (the manager uses erasable TypeScript and type-only imports):

```js
const { SaveManager } = await import('./libs/components/video-editor/src/lib/core/managers/save-manager.ts');
const editor = {
  project: {
    getActive: () => ({ metadata: { id: 'draft' } }),
    getIsLoading: () => false,
    getMigrationState: () => ({ isMigrating: false }),
    saveCurrentProject: async () => { throw new Error('disk full'); },
  },
  scenes: { subscribe: () => () => {} },
  timeline: { subscribe: () => () => {} },
};
const save = new SaveManager({ editor, debounceMs: 5 });
try { await save.flush(); } catch {}
console.log(save.getIsDirty()); // false although persistence failed
save.stop();

const auto = new SaveManager({ editor, debounceMs: 5 });
const failure = new Promise(resolve => process.once('unhandledRejection', resolve));
auto.markDirty();
console.log((await failure).message); // disk full
console.log(auto.getIsDirty()); // false

auto.stop();
```

This was executed against unchanged manager source on both pinned main and PR#2077 with a fake rejecting adapter. It is not a real IndexedDB or React UI test.

### Source and expected behavior

[`save-manager.ts`](https://github.com/storytold/artcraft/blob/d4e4ac69bbd93d237eaf5d0260bc6a5ff3a5e373/frontend/libs/components/video-editor/src/lib/core/managers/save-manager.ts) clears `hasPendingSave` before awaiting storage; `finally` clears `isSaving` without restoring pending state after failure. The timer discards the `saveNow()` promise.

Preserve an unsaved/error state and explicitly handle timer-save rejection. Continue rejecting explicit `flush()` so callers can keep the project open…
